# Slice C guard fixture: when both legacy `main/1` and `main/0` exist, the entry selector prefers `main/1`.
# Expected: `top`, then `main1`, then the entry result 11; `main/0` does not run.
# Inline documentation keeps this guard within the bounded C++ host syntax.
main(args) = "Legacy `main(args)` entry point that prints `main1` and returns 11; preferred over the zero-argument clause." { print("main1"); 11 }
main() = { print("main0"); 10 }
print("top")
42
